(text "No host power is tied to a processor rail. A1 and OE follow connector VBUS.\nB1Y reports VBUS through a divider to the dedicated detector; B2 is tied LOW.\nEither translator supply absent disables its outputs. R635 defines the detector LOW.\n\nQUALIFICATION OPEN: dedicated VBUSDET leakage/LOW threshold, rail tolerance,\npartial-supply behavior, reset timing and USB BootROM operation.\nCalculated HIGH is 2.711–3.198V only under research/recovery-qualification.json assumptions.\nThis circuit is not release-qualified; resolve these bounds before manufacture." (at 17.78 157.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "11d16807-49ca-54b0-ba60-19c0938d3d78"))
(text "USB programming port: use a USB data cable and independent board power.\nHold the recovery control during reset for Loader mode; eMMC D0 service pads provide MaskROM fallback.\nSee buttons sheet for RECOVERY / RESET / POWER controls; protected analog IO is still to be captured." (at 15.24 233.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f9e86c18-b6e7-5bb5-a520-85642e644e94"))
)
